gio: sys's views drawn by gio (gioui.org), a window beside the terminal,
and the check that sys's programs need no terminal: fm, ed and the lens
run here as they are, each at the end of a pipe (-s), and what is no
text is laid out by sys/view, the terminal's own view, whose lines this
draws as runs (`view/term.go:/Lines is the screen/`).

    gio/build             into bin/window
    gio/build test        vet and tests, on the fm, ed and studio in bin/
    window -studio .      studio's frame on the folder you are in, as
                          `studio slots` says it
    fm -w, ed -w file     one program, its view this window

sys's ./build goes first, for the tests and the window run the fm, ed
and studio in bin/. its own go module, so that sys takes on neither gio
nor cgo; it needs freetype2 and `DejaVuSansMono.ttf`, and the C headers
it builds on are unpacked into ~/.cache/sys-gio, nothing installed.

what is where
    main.go     the window: input, drawing and the frame; the one file
                that knows gio
    ft.go       text by freetype, sharp as the terminal's
    host.go     the frame's slots, a program in each
    model.go    a program as the window holds it: sys/view for a
                folder or the lens, a text drawn here
    look.go     ed's text, and sys/view's lines, as strips
    mouse.go    the three buttons and the wheel, as on the terminal

keys: ctrl-w the next pane; ctrl-v paste; f11 full screen; the other
chords, ctrl-c, -x, -z, -y and -s, are ed's, as on the terminal. a
frame's keys are as there (`studio/cheatsheet`), and on its tab line
each tab's name is a button, a click showing that tab.

mouse: as on the terminal (`design/mouse`). a drag in ed's text selects,
the wheel moves, a right click opens, and a middle click hands the word,
or the selection it falls in, to p -a. in the frame a right click on a
file says it, and ed or fm, following cur, show it, the eye going there;
what is no file opens beside. p -a lands in tmux's marked or last pane,
for the window has no shell yet.

? shows a program's keys here as rows, which esc closes, and fm's
finders, f, s and m, run fzy beside the window, in st, fm taking the
line chosen.

careful: closing the window drops what ed has not saved. q in fm asks
first, as in tmux: while ed holds work unsaved it says so, and a second q
ends the frame anyway.

not here yet
    - a shell: its slot says so. the plan runs it through tmux's control
      mode (`todo/03-studio/03-shell`)
    - v, w and F, which fm runs on its terminal (`todo/04-gio/02-term`)
